# Story 108: Browser Tools (45s)
# Hook: Navigate, click, type, screenshot -- the agent's browser toolbelt.
# Duration: 45s
# Source: story-108-browser-tools.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:05.0]
Navigate, click, type, screenshot -- the agent's browser toolbelt.

[00:05.0 --> 00:15.0]
The core tool is browser_action -- it can navigate to a URL, type into a field, or click an element on the page.

[00:15.0 --> 00:26.0]
To read the page, the agent uses get_text to pull content, and screenshot to capture the view as a base64 image it can reason over.

[00:26.0 --> 00:36.0]
It can run arbitrary page JavaScript with execute_js -- which always requires your approval -- and manage tabs: get_tabs, switch_tab, new_tab, close_tab.

[00:36.0 --> 00:45.0]
And to find elements reliably, it has six selector strategies to choose from -- so it can target the right thing even on messy pages.

